# The platform image set — the SINGLE SOURCE both substrates read (P19 Decision 2).
#
# Docker Compose reads these as env vars; the Kubernetes base pins the same digests in its
# `kustomization.yaml` `images:` block. A CI check (scripts/deploy/check-image-parity.sh) fails the
# build if the two substrates reference different digests or a different image set — so "it works on
# compose but not the cluster" is always a TOPOLOGY question, never an IMAGE question.
#
# 🔴 EVERY IMAGE IS PINNED BY DIGEST, NOT A FLOATING TAG. A tag moves; a digest is the artifact. An
# apply of the same digest twice yields the same running image, which is the reproducibility NFR9 buys.
# The `-#pin:<tag>` trailing comment records the human-readable tag the digest was cut from, for the
# release notes — it is documentation, never what is applied.
#
# The platform's own three images (agentd, console, admin-console) are pinned by the RELEASE PIPELINE
# (out of P19 scope) when it publishes them; the digests below are format-valid placeholders that the
# pipeline replaces. The backing-store images are third-party and pinned here directly. Repin any of
# them deliberately, in a commit, with the new digest recorded — never by editing a tag.

# ── Platform images ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Built for linux/arm64 (Graviton t4g nodes) and pushed to this account's ECR. The repositories are
# IMMUTABLE-tagged, so a pin can never be made to point at different bytes.
#
# ⚠️ PER IMAGE, not one commit for the file. Each pin names the tree its bytes were built from, and
# repinning an image whose code did not change would break that. The customer console stays at
# 63a3a03 (the v0.22.0 release line) because nothing since has touched it.
#
# agentd is at b5175c4 — the rehearsal-failure sentence (#106), the provider endpoint override
# (#107) and its scope split (#109), the overlay routing the gate through a relay (#110), the
# idempotency-key fix that stops every definition sharing one provider request identity (#112), and
# the rehearsal report carrying its abstentions so a fixture's zero says whether the model answered
# nothing or the validator refused everything it answered (#113). The admin console stays at 125df81: none of those touch web/, so its
# bytes did not change and repinning it would make its pin name a tree it was not built from.
#
# 🔴 agentd and the admin console were at the SAME commit for PR #105 and are not now, which is the
# point of per-image pins. #105 spanned the wire — a read-model field in agentd and the editor
# rendering it in the console — so both had to move together or the control would have been dead on
# arrival. Nothing since has touched the wire, so only agentd moves.
#
# The same coupling exists for releases: internal/api/install.go serves its install surface from
# distribution.DocumentedRelease, so a console-only push would leave the API answering the previous
# version behind a page showing the new one.
AGENTD_IMAGE=373468206837.dkr.ecr.us-east-1.amazonaws.com/agentd@sha256:e2e976c68cd700318ff52705bd89bb647b02c05175dd829714d87c8cedf5e4e4 #pin:b5175c4
CONSOLE_IMAGE=373468206837.dkr.ecr.us-east-1.amazonaws.com/heros-console@sha256:e882d793d83d442fbd1a39e7ff7fa1450ff6173105a7cd4b2cd4c30a027b751e #pin:63a3a03
ADMIN_CONSOLE_IMAGE=373468206837.dkr.ecr.us-east-1.amazonaws.com/heros-admin-console@sha256:ffc4e33b963208618744b45eb7e5a0086184c71fe39c25994a53cc24f0156a54 #pin:125df81

